    The effective resistance between s and t is related to st-connectivity by the fact that if s and t
are not connected, then Rs,t is undefined (there is no flow from s to t) and if s and t are connected
then Rs,t is related to the number and length of paths from s to t. In particular, if s and t are
connected by a path of length p, then Rs,t(G) ≤ p (take the unit flow that simply travels along this
path). In general, if s and t are connected in G, then n2 ≤ Rs,t(G) ≤ n − 1. The span program for
st-connectivity is amenable to the task of estimating the effective resistance due to the following.

